/// EventListener — protocol for actors that consume `MonitorEvent`s from
/// a `Monitor`.
///
/// In production the only implementor is `NotificationRouter`, which
/// applies dedup and fans events out to webhook channels. Tests inject
/// recording stubs that conform to the same interface so they can assert
/// on what the Monitor emitted.
///
/// Implementations should treat `handleEvent:` as fire-and-forget: the
/// Monitor sends events via `!` (cast) so it never blocks on a slow
/// listener. The return type is `Object` (rather than `Nil`) to keep the
/// signature flexible — `NotificationRouter` returns a `Boolean` that
/// indicates whether the event was forwarded or deduped.
///
/// See SPEC.md §3 (Monitor) and §5 (NotificationRouter).
Protocol define: EventListener
  /// Receive a MonitorEvent for handling (routing, logging, alerting).
  handleEvent: event :: MonitorEvent -> Object
